            "reviewer_id": "User_16714815_1_5",
            "review_title": "Review at Banh Nam",
            "review_text": "Cindy Soka\nMelbourne, Australia354 contributions\n0\nDisappointing first experience of a Banh\nFeb 2019 • Solo\nI grabbed a quick Banh Mi (Vietnamese Sandwich) from Banhnam on my way to the Cu Chi Tunnels. It is located on 213 Bùi Viện in District 1. \n\nThey have a large range of sandwich fillings. For vegetarians, they have a crispy tofu filling. I opted for “classic ham” for about 23,000 VD (under £0.76). I asked for extra cheese which I was given but not charged for. They had a special 20% off discount that day, so I got money off. \n\nYou can see the sandwich being made in front of you and you can add sauces too. Once the fillings are put into the baguette, the lady stood on her stool to put it in a grill/microwave that was above the counter to warm it slightly. Getting my Banh Mi took about 5 minutes. \n\nThe sandwich was “just ok”. It wasn’t anything special. The baguette was very flaky which made a bit of a mess on the bus. I found myself eating quickly just to avoid being covered in loads of crumbs. \n\nI was given a napkin and toothpick in my sandwich bag. \nThere were no toilet facilities. \n\nThe lady serving was perfectly polite.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten February 21, 2019",
